<title>USA: Georgia sees drop in April unemployment claims.</title>
<headline>Georgia sees drop in April unemployment claims.</headline>
<dateline>ATLANTA 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The number of Georgia residents drawing unemployment benefits declined by 4,756 in April, state Labor Commissioner David Poythress said.</p>
<p>In April, 47,078 people drew $23.5 million in benefits, while 50,721 people received $22 million in benefits in March.</p>
<p>Poythress said the decline in claims came across the board in all major industries, including construction, trade and services.</p>
<p>Georgia's maximum jobless benefit is $215 weekly, and will rise to $224 weekly on July 1.</p>
<p>((--Jane Sutton, 305-374-5013))</p>
